The Day 234 (14:42) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is gitignored, but the file is on disk where the planner reads it. The command you gave ends in || true, so this looks expected.

State: Build and tests are green: the harness checked them on HEAD ff58fa2f, and I didn't re-run the full suite. The binary reports v0.3.0 and -p answers. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and the recent evolve and CI runs all passed.

What I found:
1. There is no size limit on image files. I measured this. A --image that is just a zero-filled 30 MB file named .png pushed memory to 774 MB. A 300 MB one pushed it to 4.7 GB. Without an image, memory stayed at 31 MB. The code that reads images (read_image_for_add) loads and base64-encodes the whole file and never checks its size. Claude Code 2.1.302 shipped a 128 MB cap on image reads.
2. yoagent 0.25.10 is already in Cargo.lock, and no session has read it. It adds a lookup for model presets (ModelConfig::preset, presets(), generic()), which would replace the three preset tables yoyo maintains by hand. One gap I confirmed: yoagent has presets for glm-5.3 and glm-5.3-flash on zai, but yoyo's zai setup ignores them. Those models run on generic limits with no price. yoyo's list of known zai models still shows the old glm-4-* ids. This belongs under #1037.
3. Smaller open items:
   • #1058: undo --last-commit exits 0 when git fails. The issue has the steps to reproduce it.
   • #1054: there is still no test checking that tool results with several blocks actually reach the model in the request.
   • #1057: the hourly cleanup of /spawn work folders can delete one a running background worker still uses.
4. Other Claude Code changes: 2.1.300 handles an MCP tool whose input schema the API rejects every turn. yoyo has no equivalent, but I only read that in the changelog and didn't test yoyo against it. I saved the Claude Code 2.1.300–2.1.303 and yoagent 0.25.10 notes to yopedia.

Suggested order for the planner: image size cap first, then switching to yoagent's preset lookup, then #1058, then #1054. The outside-read fence default stays as it is until @yuanhao answers in Discussion #1048 (tracked as #1055).

