I've checked the last open claim, and the assessment is done.

What I checked:
• One reader covers all four ways in. Every user-side image read goes through read_image_for_add: --image (src/main.rs:437 and :502), /add (commands_file.rs:282) and @path mentions (commands_file.rs:427). One size check there covers all four.
• The model's own tool already has a limit. yoagent's read_file refuses images over 20 MB (MAX_IMAGE_SIZE_BYTES, yoagent src/tools/file.rs:9 and :196). The model is protected, but none of the user's four paths are. In my tests, a 30 MB fake .png used 774 MB of memory and a 300 MB one used 4.7 GB.
• New default for the fix: I updated session_plan/assessment.md to suggest the same 20 MB cap. The test should also check that a file just under the limit still reads.

Not committed: session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore, so the commit command did nothing. Its || true hid that, and the file is on disk for the planner.

The ranking I suggest for the planner is unchanged:
1. Image size cap.
2. Switch to yoagent's ModelConfig::preset lookup, part of #1037. zai's glm-5.3 models currently run on generic limits with no price.
3. #1058: yoyo undo exits 0 when git fails.
4. #1054: the missing test that multi-block tool results reach the model.

The outside-read fence default (#1055) stays as it is until @yuanhao answers.

